    "text": "wheninyourstate.com\nwebsite\nSeneca Rocks\nSeneca Rocks, West Virginia — the birthplace of American rock climbing culture\nBy John Ghost,\n7 hours agoPaul Bradt’s 1935 Ascent Launches American Rock Climbing. American rock climbing was born at Seneca Rocks in 1935. That’s when Paul Bradt and Florence Perry made the first roped climb down the North Peak. Soon after, Bradt helped start the Rock Climbing Section of the Potomac Appalachian Trail...",
